sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant TR as Test Runner
    participant FI as Failure Ingestion
    participant FR as Failure Router
    participant OR as Orchestrator
    participant Agents as Specialized Agents<br/>(Parallel)
    participant AGG as Evidence Aggregator
    participant RCA as RCA Agent
    participant MEM as Historical Memory
    participant ACT as Action Selector
    participant REC as Safe Recovery
    participant EVAL as Evaluator
    participant HITL as Human Approval
    participant OUT as Final Diagnosis

    TR->>FI: Test Failure Event
    FI->>FR: Normalized Failure Event
    FR->>FR: Structured Classification<br/>+ Confidence Score
    FR->>OR: Failure Type + Confidence

    OR->>OR: Plan Investigation Tasks

    par Parallel Evidence Collection
        OR->>Agents: Log Analysis Agent
        OR->>Agents: UI / Browser Agent
        OR->>Agents: API Agent
        OR->>Agents: Test Data Agent
        OR->>Agents: Environment Agent
        OR->>Agents: Deployment Agent
        OR->>Agents: Locator Agent
        OR->>Agents: Historical Agent
    end

    Agents->>AGG: Evidence Packets
    AGG->>RCA: Aggregated Evidence
    RCA->>MEM: Query similar historical failures
    MEM-->>RCA: Past RCA + Resolutions
    RCA->>RCA: Reason with strict layers<br/>Fact → Observation → Inference → Hypothesis → Recommendation
    RCA->>ACT: RCA Result + Confidence + Recommendation

    alt High Confidence + Low Risk
        ACT->>REC: Execute Safe Recovery Action
        REC->>EVAL: Action Result
        EVAL->>EVAL: Validate outcome
        alt Recovery Successful
            EVAL->>OUT: RESOLVED + Full Diagnosis
        else Recovery Failed / Uncertain
            EVAL->>OR: Increment counters (if limits allow)
        end
    else Low Confidence or High Risk
        ACT->>HITL: Request Human Approval
        HITL-->>ACT: Approve / Reject / Request more evidence
        alt Approved
            ACT->>REC: Execute Action
        else Rejected
            ACT->>OUT: ESCALATED with full evidence trail
        end
    end

    OUT->>MEM: Store outcome for future learning
